WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.730
Look up chlorine in the periodic table,
and its relative atomic mass is 35.45.

2
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.810
But a proton and a neutron each
have a relative mass of one,

3
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.730
and an electron adds almost nothing.

4
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.550
Count the protons and
neutrons in any one atom,

5
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.670
and you get a whole
number: its mass number.

6
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.590
No chlorine atom has a mass of 35.45.

7
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.210
So why is that the number in the table?

8
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:30.930
In this mission, you'll go inside
the atom and read its nuclear symbol,

9
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:35.830
counting the protons, neutrons
and electrons in any atom or ion.

10
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:40.050
Then you'll calculate a relative
atomic mass, step by step.

11
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.320
Your mission: explain why chlorine's
relative atomic mass isn't a whole number.
